        growth_pct=16,
        summary="Coforge delivered a strong FY26 (revenue +29.2% USD, EBIT margin +370bps to 14.4%, record $1.75bn order book, Sabre deal executing on-plan) but FY26 PAT growth of 91.6% was flattered by a Rs 244cr one-off deferred-tax credit (Cigniti-merger related) -- clean PAT growth is closer to 61-62%. The $2.35bn Encora acquisition (closed 23-Apr-2026, consolidating from May-2026) adds AI-engineering scale but brings a ~25% share-count dilution, a debt step-up to ~Rs 4,000cr FY27E, and a slower-growing, lower-margin acquired business, even as CRISIL's response was an upgrade to AA+/Stable rather than a negative-rating-watch. At a clean trailing PE near 51x (using ex-one-off PAT), the stock is not obviously cheap for FY27 organic guidance of just 13% constant-currency growth, and client/vertical concentration (top-10 clients 31.4% of revenue, BFSI+Travel+Insurance ~70%) is drifting up. With no quant score yet computed for this name, the only defensible call under V1 rules is Hold -- watch the 27/28-Jul-2026 Q1 FY27 print for the first real read on both the growth guide and Encora's blended-in numbers.",
        negative_para="FY26's headline 91.6% PAT growth is partly a tax-line artifact: a Rs 244cr deferred-tax credit (Rs 153cr in Q4 alone) tied to Cigniti-merger DTA/DTL reversal inflates reported earnings versus a clean ~61-62% PAT growth rate, and management itself guides the effective tax rate normalizing back to 23-24% in FY27-28, meaning FY27 reported profit growth optically decelerates even before any Encora effect. The Encora deal brings a ~25% imminent increase in share count (Encora holders take ~20% of expanded capital), a debt step-up from ~Rs 1,500cr to ~Rs 4,000cr guided FY27E, and a materially slower/lower-margin acquired business (~7-10% organic growth, ~19% EBITDA margin vs Coforge's own high-teens-to-20%+ growth) that will mechanically dilute blended growth as it consolidates from May-2026. On a clean (ex-one-off) EPS basis the stock trades near ~51x trailing earnings against FY27 organic guidance of just 13% constant-currency growth -- not a cheap combination -- and client/vertical concentration is drifting up (top-5 clients 21.8% vs 18.3% prior, top-10 31.4% vs 27.9%; BFSI+Insurance+Travel ~70% of FY25 revenue), leaving real discretionary-spend cyclicality exposure. GenAI-driven pricing/deflation is a genuine forward risk if large AI vendors sell equivalent tooling directly to clients, even though it is a productivity tailwind today. Q1 FY27 results (due 27/28-Jul-2026) are not yet out, so the 13% CC guide is entirely unverified as of this review.",
        positive="FY26 revenue grew 29.2% YoY in USD with EBIT margin expanding 370bps to 14.4% (Q4FY26 EBIT margin 16.6%, EBITDA margin 20.6%, both records), and the company enters FY27 with a record $1.75bn executable order book built on broad-based, multi-vertical deal wins (BFSI/healthcare/travel/Govt/insurance), not client concentration. The Sabre mega-deal -- the single largest swing factor in recent growth -- is executing ahead of cost plan per management commentary, a genuine delivery/execution positive rather than just a revenue number. The $2.35bn Encora acquisition adds real AI-engineering scale (combined ~$2.5bn revenue ambition) and diversifies the business, and CRISIL's rating response to the deal was an UPGRADE to AA+/Stable (from AA/Positive) rather than a negative watch -- a materially more comfortable credit read than comparable large-cap-IT M&A this cycle. Sell-side remains net constructive (Macquarie Outperform Rs 2,230, CLSA High-Conviction Outperform Rs 2,411, Motilal Oswal Buy Rs 1,900), and management guides the deal EPS-accretive within ~18 months on even conservative (~$20M) synergy assumptions.",
        reverse_dcf="At CMP ~Rs 1,508-1,545 (mcap ~Rs 67,900-68,000cr, mid-Jul-2026), reported trailing PE is cited anywhere from ~39x to ~48x depending on source EPS basis; forward PE is ~24.6x per GuruFocus. My own estimate: using 'clean' FY26 PAT (Rs 1,555.7cr reported minus the Rs 244cr one-off deferred-tax credit = ~Rs 1,311.7cr) against ~4.4cr shares gives clean EPS of roughly Rs 30 and a clean trailing PE closer to ~51x -- richer than most reported-EPS multiples in circulation, and this is before the ~25% Encora-driven share-count dilution further pressures per-share earnings near-term (partially offset by Encora's own EBITDA contribution once consolidated). Sustaining a ~40-50x multiple (on either basis) requires the market to underwrite continued high-teens-to-20%+ blended growth for several years; FY27 organic guidance of just 13% constant-currency growth, plus a slower-growing (~7-10% organic) Encora blending in from May-2026, makes that a harder underwrite than the FY26 print alone would suggest, even granting Coforge's real history of beating its own initial guidance. Fair value on a normalized ~15-16% three-to-five-year blended growth view (Sabre ramp normalizing, Encora drag partly offset by cross-sell/AI-engineering demand, margin near the FY27 >20.5-21% EBITDA guide) sits meaningfully below the current clean multiple -- but not so far below, nor the credit/leverage story so alarming (CRISIL upgraded, not negative-watch), as to justify a Sell call absent an actual quant score and with Q1 FY27 (the first real test of the 13% guide) still four working days from release as of this review.",
